inciples for dataplex are  around enabling you to apply governance  based on your business context and  business logic  give you the ability to Define your  governance rules based on business  context and data attributes that map to  the understanding of your data rather  than the physical storage of data  and finally give you a unified  governance platform that is open and  extensible so you can enable end-to-end  data governance across your entire data  landscape  and as a result of that you are able to  enable a data mesh architecture within  your organization that maps to your  business structure and enables  autonomous ownership of data with  centralized governance  we have a number of customers across  multiple industry verticals using  dataplex today to govern the data at  scale and make trusted data available to  drive business outcomes  when we think of governance we think of  enabling 3K key pillars for you  enabling you to discover data with  business context providing you the tools  to centrally secure and manage your data  and providing you capabilities that will  enable you to build trust in your data  now let's take a look at each one of  these in a little more detail  for discovering data with business  context you can centrally manage all  your metadata in a data catalog in  dataplex  once your data is cataloged you can now  enrich that data with relevant business  context to drive consistent  understanding of your data across your  organization  and then you can use a unified interface  to search discover  explore and share data within your  organization  dataplex already catalogs metadata from  a number of gcp sources into the central  data catalog  but we are now extending that support to  databases specifically Cloud SQL  bigtable and spanner and adding support  to catalog looker metadata  with this you have a comprehensive view  of your data from a single unified  catalog with the ability to easily  search discover  and understand your data across your  Enterprise  but oftentimes cataloging metadata is  not enough you want to enrich this data  with relevant business context  dataplex provides you the flexibility to  use stack templates to augment your  technical metadata with business  contacts  and today we are further enhancing the  business enrichment capabilities Within  dataplex by introducing two new  capabilities a business glossary that  will enable your data stewards and  subject matter experts to Define  standardized business terms and  taxonomies that can then be applied to  your data by all the data teams within  your organization  and Rich Text documentation that can  provide a way for your teams to create a  shared understanding of your data by  crowdsourcing and collaborating on Rich  business contexts and storing that right  within the catalog as part of the  metadata of a given entry instead of in  wikis and personal nodes across your  organization  together these features along with  existing features such as stack  templates help you create a shared and  common understanding of your data within  your organization and enable your teams  to effectively use share and collaborate  over data  in addition to Discovery and enrichment  dataplex also provides a data  exploration workbench  this workbench gives your data consumers  one-click access to spark SQL and  notebooks with the ability to save their  work share their work and collaborate  across teams  as well as operationalize their work  with one-click scheduling built right  into the workbench  it also gives your data admins the  ability to pre-configure and Define the  environments for different teams and use  cases  your data admins can govern access to  these environments track usage and  attribute consumption per user or team  across your organization  today this feature is available in  preview and it will be generally  available soon  now let's move to the next pillar around  centrally securing and managing your  data  with dataplex you can secure access to  your data using business contacts  instead of uh instead of terminology  that Maps your underlying infrastructure  you can provide secure access to your  data  across your organization in a way where  you're enabling distributed ownership of  the data while still having centralized  governance so let's take a closer look  in dataplex you can logically organize  your data by defining data domains and  sub-domains and then map your Access  Control policies at the Domain level  across distributed data  dataplex will then take these policies  and map to the underlying physical  resources  propagate them at scale  to data that is stored in different  storage products  as well as across different gcp projects  you can easily designate data owners  producers and admins and have teams  self-manage their data while still  having the ability to Monitor and audit  all actions centrally as well as apply  certain governance policies across all  your data domains  in addition to defining policies at the  Domain level  we are now introducing the ability to  create attributes and Define your  business taxonomy within the dataplex  attributes tool and then Define your  governance policies based on these  attributes  as an example you can easily Define  different data classes like pii data map  the attributes that are considered pii  within your organization and Define  policies associated with that  we are starting with Access Control  policies which dataplex will then map to  the tables and columns and apply them at  scale to data in GCS and bigquery we  have bigquery tables and Big Lake tables  this feature will be available in  preview in the in the early part of 2023  in addition to policy propagation we're  also enhancing our existing GCS data  Discovery capability by now adding  support to create big lake and object  tables at scale  so what does that actually mean  instead of creating bigquery connections  and big league tables one table at a  time you can simply Point your GCS  buckets where your analytics data  resides to dataplex and dataplex will  automatically set up the connections  create both big league tables for  structured data and object tables for  unstructured data and keep this data and  metadata in sync as new data arrives  dataplex will also make this available  as part of the data catalog so that this  data is easily discoverable and  accessible to your teams  and finally let's look at how dataplex  can help you build trust in your data by  getting that 360 View and understanding  of your data improving data reliability  and enabling you to have better data  obserability  so the First new capability that will  help you build better trust in your data  is automatic data profiling and data  quality  with automatic data profiling you can  profile your data and have that profile  be available alongside your metadata  you can then use that profile to Auto  generate data quality rules  and run them at scale on a fully managed  serverless platform  you can check for things like  completeness accuracy validity and  freshness  as well as add your own custom rules for  custom checks that you want to enable on  your data  you can track the your data quality  metrics at a granular level  at a specific table level within  dataplex or within bigquery  to ensure that the data that you're  using meets your data Quality Bar  but you can also monitor the overall  health of your data with built-in  dashboards and reports that will be  available Within dataplex  and finally in addition to monitoring  your data quality you can also set up  built-in actions to quarantine data that  does not meet your data quality  thresholds  so for that we are announcing the  general availability of lineage which  will be available in early part of 2023.  our goal is to provide you end-to-end  data lineage with automatic processing  of lineage for gcp sources and  extensibility to third-party sources  lineage is available alongside the rest  of the metadata and dataplex so you can  trace the origins of your data to its  upstream and downstream relationships  and use it to understand your data  better  identify data issues and use lineage as  a foundation to apply your governance  and compliance policies  we are starting with bigquery which is  the lineage for which is currently in  preview and will be available uh in  general availability in q1 of 2023  and we are also extending that support  to composer and data Fusion so you can  track your lineage across your data  integration and data movement pipelines  in addition to your analytics store  and in addition to that we are also  making our lineage apis available so you  can embed them in your own custom tools  and ingest lineage into dataplex  and that's all I have for you today I  went through many different capabilities  that will be available to you in the  coming months in each one of these three  pillars to really help you discover your  data with business context  centrally secure and manage your data  and build trust in your data so that you  can govern your data at scale  to learn more please visit these  additional resources as well as visit  our product page listed at the bottom  and thank you for your time today and I  hope you have a great rest of next 22.  [Music]

